  The fork: whether we introduce a module system now, or stay with the global-script style [38;5;153mapp.js[39m already uses.

  - [1mGlobal namespace module[0m — a new [38;5;153msession.js[39m loaded before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, exposing something like [38;5;153mwindow.Session = { [39m
    [38;5;153msetUserId, getUserId, clear }[39m. Buys one place that owns the storage key and the value's shape, with no build step,
    and [38;5;153mindex.html[39m still opens directly from disk. Costs a global and an implicit script-tag ordering dependency.
    Matches what's already in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m.
  - [1mES modules[0m — [38;5;153m<script type="module">[39m, [38;5;153msession.js[39m exports real functions, [38;5;153mapp.js[39m imports them. Buys proper scoping and
    no globals. Costs a local dev server: module scripts are blocked over [38;5;153mfile://[39m, so opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m by
    double-clicking stops working. That's a new tooling requirement for a repo that currently has none.
  - [1mNo module — each form touches [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m directly.[0m Buys the least code today. Costs the exact thing you said you
    wanted to avoid: the key name and the value shape get copy-pasted into every new form, and they drift.

  [1mMy recommendation: the global namespace module.[0m It matches the existing style, keeps the app runnable with no server
  or build, and still gives you the single owner of the key that "other forms will need it later" is really asking for.
  ES modules are the better long-term structure, but they only pay for themselves if you expect a build step here anyway
  — and right now there isn't one to extend.

  Note on the third option: I'm listing it for completeness, not recommending it. It's the status quo scaled up, and
  it's what your requirement rules out.

  To be clear about what I'm [3mnot[0m touching: [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m are a separate CommonJS Node entry point with
  no connection to the browser app. I'll leave them alone unless you tell me otherwise.
